# Identity and Access

> Status: Current operator guide for authentication, authorization, and tenancy.
> Sections marked **Planned** describe work tracked in
> [the identity-and-access plan](exec-plans/active/identity-and-access.md) and
> are not available yet.

Caesium supports API keys for machines and optional browser SSO for interactive
users. SSO is additive: keep `CAESIUM_AUTH_MODE=api-key` enabled and turn on one
or more providers with `CAESIUM_AUTH_OIDC_ENABLED`,
`CAESIUM_AUTH_SAML_ENABLED`, or `CAESIUM_AUTH_LDAP_ENABLED`. Who may do what is
decided by roles granted per namespace, either from an access policy file
(recommended) or from the legacy `CAESIUM_AUTH_ROLE_MAPPING` variable.

